 {"id":"fabro-78ac","title":"engine: fabro_run_create swallows the created run id when start fails (partial success reported as total failure)","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:25:09.559Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T08:15:16.548Z","description":"create_runs_with_options does create-then-start with ?-propagation: when create succeeds (201, run exists pending) but start_run fails (e.g. approval_required 409), the ENTIRE tool call returns an error and the created run id is discarded. The calling agent believes the create failed and reasonably retries — producing duplicate parallel children (observed in conductor pass 01M1S5D9XC: children 01M1S5MWDT swallowed + 01M1S5RTW8 retried 8s later; both approved by a human, serialization broken, manual cleanup). Fix: report partial success — return the created run with its state (e.g. 'created <id>, start blocked: approval_required') so callers can poll/approve instead of recreating. Complements auto_approve (7fda51235), the one-child prompt rule (3479aa998), and the approval-TTL seed fabro-54f0. Basis: run 01M1S5D9XC events 16:13:24/16:13:32, commit context 3479aa998.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"closedAt":"2026-09-06T08:15:16.548Z","closeReason":"Implemented and landed via PR #28 (b1b6df41f, run 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN): CreatedRunResult.start_error carries 'start blocked: <reason>' verbatim, create-then-start reports partial success keeping the created run id, text summary reports start-blocked count, tests cover start_error/retrieve_error paths. Seed stayed open after closeout (same class as fabro-d936 silent tracker-write failures)."}
 {"id":"fabro-e4ac","title":"engine: verbose tool-argument validation errors — name the failing field and expected shape","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:38:13.397Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:41.115Z","description":"engine: verbose tool-argument validation errors — name the failing field and expected shape. EVIDENCE (2nd incident same day, pass 01M1V9DXW8 merge@1, 12:03): the runs-wrapped spec {workflow_source, environment, auto_approve} failed 'not valid under any of the schemas listed in the anyOf keyword' NINE times — the real cause was the missing REQUIRED field CreateRunSpec.workflow (slug). Naming 'missing required property: workflow at runs[0]' would have solved attempt 1. The 11:30 pass succeeded only because its final attempt coincidentally included the slug.","labels":["engine","agent"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-571e","title":"engine: fabro_run_wait blocking tool — wait for a child run's terminal state without agent-side sleep loops","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:48:27.981Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T09:45:37.001Z","description":"Blocking fabro_run_wait tool {run_id, until: 'terminal' | 'merged', timeout_ms} — deterministic replacement for ALL agent-side wait loops (user decision 2026-09-05: option b; forks resolved 2026-09-06): (F1) timeout expiry returns structured {reached: timeout, status}; (F2) merged detection SERVER-side via PR state (RunProjection PR link, no git in the tool); (F3) server long-poll GET /runs/{id}/wait?until&timeout_ms + thin tool wrapper; ClientBackend uses send_api_long_poll so the 30s control-plane timeout cannot preempt the wait deadline. DIVISION OF LABOR (ADR-0016, user decision 2026-09-06): keep BOTH wait tools — fabro_run_wait = single run, long waits, merge integration (conductor legs); fabro_run_gather = multi-run fan-in, short bounds (revisor select). Cross-refs in tool descriptions (fabro-tool common.rs), docs (child-runs.mdx, mcp.mdx). IMPLEMENTED 2026-09-06 locally (user-assigned bootstrapping exception): OpenAPI path+RunWaitResult schema, server handler wait.rs (store poll 1.5s, GitHub poll 10s, per-call GitHub timeout 15s, deadline-bounded), fabro-client Client::wait_run + send_api_long_poll, fabro-tool wait.rs tool + validation + strum RunWaitReached, workflow dispatch arm + mock, conductor graph allowlists + 3 leg prompts (create->wait->route), integration tests (server: 4; tool: validation; workflow: dispatch).","labels":["engine","workflows","agent"],"closedAt":"2026-09-06T09:45:37.001Z","closeReason":"Landed (locally, user-assigned bootstrapping exception): server long-poll GET /runs/{id}/wait (until=terminal|merged, timeout_ms<=3.6e6; store poll 1.5s, GitHub poll 10s, per-call GitHub timeout 15s, structured reached=terminal|merged|closed_unmerged|timeout); fabro-client Client::wait_run + send_api_long_poll (bypasses 30s control-plane timeout); fabro-tool fabro_run_wait (validation, strum RunWaitReached, ADR-0016 cross-ref descriptions); workflow dispatch + registration (not inspects-gated); conductor graph allowlists + develop/merge/revise legs collapse to create->wait->route. Verification: 4 server integration tests, tool unit tests, workflow dispatch test, catalog/registration tests updated, clippy clean, 915/915 server + 1641/1642 workflow/tool/client suites (1 unrelated flaky timeout). Division of labor with fabro_run_gather per ADR-0016."}
-{"id":"fabro-94e8","title":"engine: run-branch PRs go stale when the base moves (auto-rebase or merge-queue needed for autonomous loops)","status":"in_progress","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:04:02.448Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T16:02:19.502Z","description":"Run-branch PRs go stale when the base moves between PR open and auto-merge. FRESH GUARD EVIDENCE (2026-09-06): while rescue PR #31 sat BLOCKED on a re-running dogfood gate, the next conductor pass spawned ANOTHER MergeUpstream child (01M1VGCE2AJ) for the same upstream delta — manually cancelled by the pass-guard. The survey leg has no open-run-PR awareness: a pending/mergeable run PR must suppress new merge children (or 94e8's update mechanism makes the existing PR converge). DESIGN SETTLED (grill 2026-09-06, Q1-Q5): (Q1) GitHub update-branch API from the PR supervisor (fabro_github::update_pull_request_branch, 422=conflict signal); (Q2) supervisor poll 5min over open run-linked PRs with mergeable=false; (Q3) 422/conflict -> PR stays, fabro_run_wait until=merged returns closed_unmerged/timeout, conductor routes manual; (Q4) cap 3 failed updates OR PR older than 24h -> close stale_base + run event; (Q5) develop workflow implements. Acceptance: httpmock wire tests incl. 422; supervisor updates dirty run-linked PRs only; cap/age close + event; clippy+fmt clean; nextest suites green. Basis: PR #28 (stranded DIRTY, manual repair a98db89f2, pass 01M1S6MSV4), PR #31 guard incident, mx-5141c6, pull_request_supervisor.rs seam, ADR-0016 synergy.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro"}
